--TEST--
`Core\Test::assertMatchesInline`'s failure quotes the rendering it produced beside the snapshot it was given, including the empty snapshot § 14's workflow starts from — `rule:testing/failure-ledger` and `rule:testing/inline-snapshots`, ADR 0063 R2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A snapshot's failure has to say both halves: what the value rendered as is
// the thing the author is about to accept, and the snapshot on record is what
// they are accepting it *over*. One of the two alone would leave a reader
// diffing by hand against a value they cannot see.

use Core\Test;

// 1. Both sides, quoted.
try {
    Test::assertMatchesInline(7, "int(8)");
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $offByOne) {
    echo $offByOne->message, "\n";
}

// 2. The empty snapshot is the state § 14's own workflow begins in -- the
// author writes it and asks the runner to fill it in -- so it is a mismatch
// like any other rather than a value that matches anything.
try {
    Test::assertMatchesInline("a", "");
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $unfilled) {
    echo $unfilled->message, "\n";
}

// 3. A rendering that spans lines is quoted with its line breaks written out,
// which is what keeps a multi-line snapshot's failure on one line of a report.
try {
    Test::assertMatchesInline([1], "int(1)");
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $container) {
    echo $container->message, "\n";
}

// 4. ADR 0063 R2's bag sits in front of this report as in front of every other.
try {
    Test::assertMatchesInline(true, "bool(false)", {message: "the summary is stable"});
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $withMessage) {
    echo $withMessage->message, "\n";
}

// 5. And the assertion that holds says nothing at all.
Core\Test::assertMatchesInline("a", "string(1) \"a\"");
echo "held\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Test::assertMatchesInline failed: the rendering is "int(7)", and the snapshot holds "int(8)"
Core\Test::assertMatchesInline failed: the rendering is "string(1) \"a\"", and the snapshot holds ""
Core\Test::assertMatchesInline failed: the rendering is "array(1) [\n  0 => int(1)\n]", and the snapshot holds "int(1)"
the summary is stable: Core\Test::assertMatchesInline failed: the rendering is "bool(true)", and the snapshot holds "bool(false)"
held
